===== packages/auxiliary/website_public/docs/documentation/browse_files.md
# Browse files and folders
<!-- generated by docs:update_by_ai -->
<!-- page type: how-to -->
Find files and folders in the selected workspace and control which folders are open in the Files sidebar section.
## Browse the folder tree
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/glossary.md -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/components/FilesPanel.vue -->
1. Open the **Files** sidebar section for a workspace that is a Git repository.
2. Click a folder to fold or unfold it.
3. Click a file to select its row and open it in the large Git window.
Folders appear before files, and both are listed alphabetically.
## Refresh or fold the tree
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/glossary.md -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/components/FilesPanel.vue -->
Select **Refresh** to read the folder tree again, or select **Collapse all folders** to fold every folder.
## Troubleshooting
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/glossary.md -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/components/FilesPanel.vue -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/filesPanel.json -->
### The Files sidebar section says the workspace is not a Git repository
**Cause**: The selected workspace is not a Git repository.
**Solution**:
1. Select a workspace that is a Git repository.
2. Open the **Files** sidebar section.
**Check**: The folder tree appears.
## Related pages
- [Files sidebar section](/documentation/files_sidebar_reference): to look up the tree and its controls.
- [Open a file](/documentation/open_a_file): to view a file in the large Git window.
- [Create a file or folder](/documentation/create_a_file_or_folder): to add an empty item.
===== packages/auxiliary/website_public/docs/documentation/change_the_files_list_appearance.md
# Change the Files list appearance
<!-- generated by docs:update_by_ai -->
<!-- page type: how-to -->
Adjust the indentation, row height, and indent guides in the Files sidebar section.
## Choose the list appearance
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/glossary.md -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/components/FilesPanel.vue -->
1. Select **More options** in the Files sidebar section.
2. Under **Indentation**, choose **Small**, **Medium**, or **Large**.
3. Under **Row height**, choose **Compact** or **Comfortable**.
4. Under **Indent guides**, choose **Show** or **Hide**.
## Related pages
- [Browse files and folders](/documentation/browse_files): to find files in the folder tree.
- [Files sidebar section](/documentation/files_sidebar_reference): to look up the available choices.
- [Create a file or folder](/documentation/create_a_file_or_folder): to add an item to the tree.
===== packages/auxiliary/website_public/docs/documentation/copy_a_file_path.md
# Copy a file path
<!-- generated by docs:update_by_ai -->
<!-- page type: how-to -->
Copy either the absolute path of a file or its path relative to the selected workspace.
## Copy a file path
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/glossary.md -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/components/FilesPanel.vue -->
1. In the Files sidebar section, right-click a file row.
2. Select **Copy absolute path** or **Copy relative path**.
3. Paste the copied path where you need it.
Heidrun shows the copied path in a message.
## Related pages
- [Browse files and folders](/documentation/browse_files): to find a file.
- [Open a file](/documentation/open_a_file): to view a file in the large Git window.
- [Files sidebar section](/documentation/files_sidebar_reference): to look up what the tree shows.
===== packages/auxiliary/website_public/docs/documentation/create_a_file_or_folder.md
# Create a file or folder
<!-- generated by docs:update_by_ai -->
<!-- page type: how-to -->
Create an empty file or folder in the repository of the selected workspace.
## Choose where to create the item
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/glossary.md -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/components/FilesPanel.vue -->
Select a folder to create the item there, or select a file to create the item in that file's folder. With no row selected, the item goes in the repository root.
## Create the file or folder
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/glossary.md -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/components/FilesPanel.vue -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/filesPanel.json -->
1. Select **New file** or **New folder** in the Files sidebar section.
2. Enter a name without `/` and press **Enter**.
The new row is selected. A new file also opens in the large Git window.
## Troubleshooting
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/glossary.md -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/components/FilesPanel.vue -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/filesPanel.json -->
### The name box stays open after Enter
**Cause**: The name contains `/` or already exists in the selected folder.
**Solution**:
1. Remove `/` from the name or choose a name that is not already in the folder.
2. Press **Enter**.
**Check**: The new row appears in the folder tree and is selected.
## Related pages
- [Browse files and folders](/documentation/browse_files): to find the destination folder.
- [Files sidebar section](/documentation/files_sidebar_reference): to look up the header controls.
- [Open a file](/documentation/open_a_file): to open a file from the folder tree.
===== packages/auxiliary/website_public/docs/documentation/files_sidebar_reference.md
# Files sidebar section
<!-- generated by docs:update_by_ai -->
<!-- page type: reference -->
Look up what the Files sidebar section shows and what its controls do.
## Folder tree
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/glossary.md -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/components/FilesPanel.vue -->
The tree shows files tracked by Git and new files. Folders appear before files, and each group is listed alphabetically. A changed file has a status letter at the right of its row, and a folder containing changes has a dot.
## Header buttons
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/glossary.md -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/components/FilesPanel.vue -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/filesPanel.json -->
| Name | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| **New file** | Starts creating an empty file in the selected folder, the folder of the selected file, or the repository root. |
| **New folder** | Starts creating an empty folder in the selected folder, the folder of the selected file, or the repository root. |
| **Refresh** | Reads the folder tree again. |
| **Collapse all folders** | Folds every folder. |
| **More options** | Opens the choices for indentation, row height, and indent guides. |
## More options
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/components/FilesPanel.vue -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/filesPanel.json -->
| Name | Choices |
| --- | --- |
| **Indentation** | **Small**, **Medium**, or **Large** |
| **Row height** | **Compact** or **Comfortable** |
| **Indent guides** | **Show** or **Hide** |
## Selecting rows
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/glossary.md -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/components/FilesPanel.vue -->
Clicking a file or folder selects its row; only one row is selected for the current workspace. Click empty space in the Files sidebar section to clear the selection.
## Opening files
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/glossary.md -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/components/FilesPanel.vue -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/components/GitModal.vue -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/gitModal.json -->
Clicking a file opens it in the large Git window. An unchanged file appears as a whole file, with **Diff** and **Side by side** disabled.
## Troubleshooting
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/user_interface/sidebars/files.md -->
<!-- source: docs/agents_rules/glossary.md -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/components/FilesPanel.vue -->
<!-- source: packages/apps/web_frontend/src/i18n/locales/en/filesPanel.json -->
### The Files sidebar section says the workspace is not a Git repository
**Cause**: The selected workspace is not a Git repository.
**Solution**:
1. Select a workspace that is a Git repository.
2. Open the **Files** sidebar section.
**Check**: The folder tree appears.
## Related pages
- [Browse files and folders](/documentation/browse_files): to find a file or folder.
- [Open a file](/documentation/open_a_file): to view a file in the large Git window.
- [Copy a file path](/documentation/copy_a_file_path): to copy a file path.
